# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository.
#
# Not cosmetic. The dashboard is now rebuilt and committed by CI on every green
# push to main. CI runs on Linux and writes LF; a Windows checkout writes CRLF.
# Without this the two disagree on 301 lines of an otherwise BYTE-IDENTICAL
# file, so every CI run commits "changes" that are nothing but line endings, and
# every local rebuild commits them straight back — an endless ping-pong of no-op
# commits, and the real signal ("did the dashboard actually change?") lost
# inside it. That happened once, in e96d907, which is why this file exists.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated artefacts that must be byte-identical across platforms, since the
# publish step compares them.
*.html text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.gguf binary
*.db binary
